<title>UK: Ex-dividends to take 5.524 points off FTSE, June 2.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends to take 5.524 points off FTSE, June 2.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE-100 stocks will go ex-dividend on Monday and analysts estimate the effect will be to take 5.524 points off the index at the start of trading on June 2.</p>
<p>					  DIVIDEND     INDEX</p>
<p>					    (PENCE)	EFFECT</p>
<p>   COMPANY				Net   Gross    Gross</p>
<p> * Bass PLC			    8.30  10.375    0.529</p>
<p> * British Airways		  10.80  13.500    0.783</p>
<p> * LucasVarity			 2.25   2.812    0.233</p>
<p> * Imperial Tobacco		  7.20   9.000    0.270</p>
<p> * Land Securities		  19.65  24.563    0.737</p>
<p> * Mercury Asset Management     35.00  43.750    0.481</p>
<p> * National Power		   19.00  23.750    1.686</p>
<p> * PowerGen			   17.40  21.750    0.805</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
